TITLE:: REVisualsTape
summary:: What a piece sends to HomewareVisuals, with the time of each message
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/RCVisuals, Classes/REOfflineTap, Classes/RERenderedPlayer

DESCRIPTION::
The messages link::Classes/RCVisuals:: sends (notes, births, cycles, lines, the score feed...) with the second of each, in the format HomewareVisuals' code::scripts/viz-record.mjs:: records from the bridge: code::[[seconds, "/address", arg, ...], ...]::, plain JSON, one entry per line, Symbols as strings (the pages read plain strings). A render records one through RCVisuals' sink with the offline clock's seconds (link::#*record::), shifts it to the take's start, the WAV's timeline (link::#-shifted::), and writes it next to the render's WAV as code::<take>/<take>.viz.json:: (link::Classes/REScore::'s code::tapePath::) (HomewareSC's code::scripts/take.sh render --viz::; the state taps' frames are merged in by its Python side, link::Classes/REOfflineTap::). A rendered take played live (link::Classes/RERenderedPlayer::) plays the tape back through RCVisuals (link::#-play::), and a page plays one alone with code::?replay=<url>::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: record
A new tape recording: the sink installed (the previous one kept, put back by link::#-finish::), every message with code::timeFunc.value:: as its time.
argument:: timeFunc
The seconds of a message (the calling thread's seconds by default; a render gives its offline clock's).

METHOD:: read
The file read back: the times and the numbers as numbers, the strings as strings, code::null:: as nil. Nil when the file is missing or is not a tape. The file is read whole and cut into pieces of about link::#*chunkBytes:: at line ends, each compiled as an sclang literal array (a JSON array of numbers and strings is one; the compiler types the numbers): a 323 MB tape of 46 million values reads in about 5 s (it took 3 minutes through code::String:parseJSON::, whose scalars are all Strings). A piece with JSON's code::\u:: escapes (Python's code::json.dumps::) or one the compiler refuses goes through code::parseJSON::. The file is compiled: read the tapes you made. The last link::#*cacheSize:: tapes read are kept, by path, size, date and options: reading one again answers a tape of its own on the same entries at once.
argument:: path
argument:: skip
Addresses left out (Strings or Symbols).
argument:: rate
code::(address: frames a second)::: an address's entries thinned per first argument (a tap's frames: code::/lsys/state::'s start slot), e.g. code::('/lsys/state': 10)::.

METHOD:: load
The same as link::#*read::, in a Routine on AppClock that yields between two pieces, so that the interpreter goes on scheduling meanwhile (progress posted every tenth). Returns the Routine.
argument:: path
argument:: skip
argument:: rate
argument:: action
code::{ |tape| }:: at the end (nil when the file is not a tape).

METHOD:: clearCache
Forgets the tapes read.
METHOD:: cacheSize
The tapes kept (2).
METHOD:: chunkBytes
The text compiled at once (1 MB): a load yields between two.
METHOD:: reads
The files parsed so far (not the cache's answers).

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: record
METHOD:: finish
The previous sink back.
METHOD:: isRecording

METHOD:: add
argument:: secs
argument:: path
argument:: args
METHOD:: addEntries
Entries from elsewhere (the state taps' frames), added and sorted in.
METHOD:: sort
METHOD:: entries
METHOD:: size
METHOD:: isEmpty
METHOD:: duration
The last entry's seconds.
METHOD:: countBy
Address → count.
METHOD:: shifted
A new tape with every time minus code::secs::, clamped at 0.
argument:: secs

METHOD:: write
argument:: path
returns:: The path.

METHOD:: play
A Routine on the clock: code::atSecs:: is the time of the tape's 0, each entry sent at code::atSecs:: plus its seconds through code::RCVisuals.sendArgs::, or to code::func.(path, args)::.
argument:: atSecs
The clock's seconds the tape's 0 stands at (now when nil): on SystemClock, the logical seconds a take's player starts at, less the seconds of its code::from::.
argument:: clock
SystemClock; an link::Classes/REOfflineClock:: in a test.
argument:: func
argument:: from
The tape's seconds to start from: the entries before it are skipped and the Routine begins at code::atSecs + from:: (a take played from a later beat: link::Classes/RERenderedPlayer::).
returns:: The Routine.
METHOD:: stop
METHOD:: isPlaying

EXAMPLES::

code::
// a render (scripts/sc/take_render.scd)
t = REVisualsTape.record({ clock.seconds });
... clock.advanceTo(endBeat) ...
t.finish;
t.shifted(startSecs).write(out.drop(-4) ++ ".viz.json");

// a page preview without sound: HomewareVisuals' public/recordings/<name>.json, then
// http://localhost:5173/Personal_SC/.../HadronLake3_LSystemViz_w0_260929.html?replay=/recordings/<name>.json

// played back live by hand (RERenderedPlayer does this with the WAV)
t = REVisualsTape.read(path);
t.play(thisThread.seconds + 1);
t.stop;
::
